criptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-10T14:11:30Z","updated_at":"2020-01-10T14:11:30Z","body":"Laurent this brings up a very good question though. When unix_cc_configure.bzl is in rules_cc which is a workspace rule, how do we introduce incompatible changes if we cannot create Starlark semantic flags from outside? Even if rules_cc is outside of Bazel I expect that due to its importance we will still be asked to follow the same policy, but how would we do this?\r\n\r\n1) unix_cc_configure.bzl is in Bazel for now. \r\n2) But even when it's in rules_cc, we will have to add incompatible flags through Bazel until a mechanism for incompatible changes in external repositories is available. \r\n\r\nSo this incorrectness bug due to workspaces not being refetched should be prioritized anyway starting with 1)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/573050349/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"oquenchil","id":23365806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzY1ODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23365806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil","html_url":"https://github.com/oquenchil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquenchil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oquen